A||||8||88formula||Has anyone here dyno tested the FOCOA headers? Need your help and opinions. ||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||04-22-2001||02:50 PM||||I'm looking for a header that takes advantage of wave dynamics or suction waves to help scavenge the exhaust gases out of the cylinder like a true header should. I know the sprint manifolds are not much better than stock ported manifolds. The Chris West units have been dynoed by 1FST2M6 and didn't make any real power gains over the stock manifolds. In fact he lost most of his low end torque, which shouldn’t happen if the header is a tuned header. I'm wondering if the FOCOA headers are any better.<P>Thanks in advance guys.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroparts.com||04-22-2001||02:59 PM||||I think Chris West made the ones for FOCOA?||||reg||14
Z||000002||Shaun41178||04-22-2001||03:57 PM||||No Chris West didn't make them.  I don't know who did but I can tell you that I have seen dyno results from the FOCOA headers.  No they do not give 20 hp on a 2.8  THey gave an increase of 7-10 peak of 7-10 if I remember correctly.  However I am certain it was not more then 10 hp.  Increases might be more if on a 3.4 or a 3.2 as this dyno was from a 2.8 with more then 50k on it so perhaps take that into account.  <P>The dyno sheet is up on the web somewhere but I don't remember the address<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||jlruiz67||04-22-2001||04:49 PM||||Originaly posted by Pretender<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001019-2-002583.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001019-2-002583.html</A> <P>posted 03-06-2000 03:55 PM              <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Well I called and placed an order for a set! I got the uncoated ones, the coated ones were $190 more. They were $550. Plus $45 for shipping. Phil was very nice and seemed very knowledgable. Also he claimed a dyno figure of +25HP. but thats probably at the motor? eitherway I'll tell you guys all about how the install goes and the 1/4 mile times that I get. I'd like to thank the IRS for making this possable(GO REFUND!). talk to you guys later, shawn. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||04-22-2001||05:23 PM||||Ten horsepower measured at the wheels is pretty good if the 2.8-liter engine was the stock motor with the stock camshaft. Could you dig up those dyno results for me or give me a little more insight on what the dyno figures were?<P>Being that the fiero does not use a mass air flow sensor the headers would change the air fuel ratio of the engine because the engine would pump more air but not give it more fuel. If the person did not compensate for this by changing the calibrations of the prom chip than the full potential of the headers might not be realized. Am I right?<P><BR>Thanks for your help.<P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||04-22-2001||08:21 PM||||The computer is more flexable then people<BR>would have you believe but an aftermarket<BR>chip will also help the computer "understand"<BR>a little better. ;-)<BR>However, a custom chip will give you the full<BR>potential of your mods.<BR>If you go with radical mods. like forced ind.<BR>or a very radical cam then you more than likely will experience probs. and need a<BR>custom chip just to make it run.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||04-22-2001||08:44 PM||||Being that the fiero does not use a mass air flow sensor the headers would change the air fuel ratio of the engine. It would go lean. If the person did not compensate for this by changing the calibrations of the prom chip than the full potential of the headers might not be realized on a stock engine. Often times too total ignition timing can be backed off with a free flowing exhaust system and you would gain more power.<P>The correct air fuel ratio along with the correct ignition timing might make the ten horsepower gain a twenty horsepower gain right?  <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tryxalon||04-22-2001||11:00 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jlruiz67:<BR><B>I'd like to thank the IRS for making this possable(GO REFUND!). </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So the IRS <B>finally (6-12 months later) </B> gives you back the change from overcharging you and you <I> thank them?? </I> Do you also let the waitress hold your change until the next time you visit the restaurant??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Well, I guess the IRS could have just kept it, couldn't they?? <P>Glad you found the funds to get your headers!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P> <p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
